ple of magipore are on high alert  and wastes no time coming after sam  bucky and zemo  the trio seems done for but they're  saved in the nick of time by former  shield agent sharon carter who reveals  what she's been up to since her last mcu  appearance in captain america  civil war in the 2016 film she's shown  stealing both  sam's falcon wings and the captain  america shield for steve rogers from the  united states government they'd been  confiscated since the heroes were  branded criminals for choosing not to  sign the sokovia accords for helping  them sharon was labeled an enemy of the  state and had no choice but to escape  the us  her travels led her to madrapore where  she's built an impressive life for  herself  sharon goes above and beyond to help sam  bucky and zemo find their next target  the man responsible for creating the new  super soldier serum and then helps them  stay alive long enough to flee madrapore  however rather than join them for the  next stop on their quest sharon decides  to stay put  while sam promised to get her pardoned  upon the mission's completion until it  goes through she's still a wanted  fugitive  sharon carter has a long history in the  comics as an ally of captain america but  her time in madripore may have led her  to prioritize her own well-being  we'll have to see whether she pops up  again as a friend or foe to bucky or sam  so far luck hasn't been on sam and  bucky's side when it comes to finding  carly morgenthau and the rest of the  flag smashers  the next best thing would be to find  who's responsible for the return of the  super soldier serum something that zemo  manages to uncover during his  negotiations with selby  before she's killed she tells them that  the person producing it is named dr  wilfred nagel a scientist who works for  the mysterious power broker  and has gone to horrendous lengths to  replicate dr erskine's formula  thanks to sharon's connections in  madrapore's underworld she discovers his  secret lab's location hidden inside a  series of shipping containers  as dr nagel explains to sam bucky and  zemo after they enter his lab hydra  recruited him to revitalize the  long dormant winter soldier program  however his career faced a shift  when hydra collapsed and he then went to  work with the cia  during that time dr nagel used the blood  samples of unsung super soldier isaiah  bradley to successfully recreate and  further refine the serum unfortunately  for him he disappeared in thanos  infamous snap returning five years later  to find the cia  no longer had use for his research bent  on completing his work dr nagel came to  madripore with none other than the power  broker as his financial backer before  sam and bucky can get any more  information out of dr nagle zemo shoots  and  kills him there's good and bad that  comes out of dr nagle's death the good  is that he can't make any more super  soldier serum and  unless someone else also knows how to  create it sam bucky and zemo now have  something of an edge in their mission  the bad of course is that they won't get  any more answers or leads from the  scientist  while our heroes attempt to crack the  case of these super soldier serums  re-emergents we learn a bit more about  flag smashers figurehead carly  morgenthau it's revealed that she has a  strong connection to someone she refers  to as mama dania madini who dies toward  the end of the episode from tuberculosis  carly uses this loss to fuel her mission  of helping those whose lives have been  disrupted and who've been displaced  since half the world's population  returned from the blip  it sounds like a noble enough cause but  her methods are questionable at best  not only did carly steal all of the  power broker's remaining doses of super  soldier serum but she and the flag  smashers are also now using it to spread  chaos wherever they go  even after stripping a global  repatriation council shelter of its  stockpiled resources carly uses a car  bomb to send the building up in flames  while the grc's people are still inside  she claims that doing so is the only way  to get those opposed to the flag  smashers cause to listen but even  carly's ally dovich is taken aback by  this new level of violence  viewers don't see much of john walker  this week but what they do get is quite  revealing  he's first shown infiltrating a  suspected flagsmasher's refuge and  almost  immediately losing his cool on the man  who owns the building walker attempts to  use his status as captain america to  threaten him  going as far as using physical force to  interrogate him and when it doesn't work  walker fumes later on we see walker  speak with lamar hoskins about their  plan to stop the anarchist group  lamar if we get the job done do you  really think they're going to sweat us  on the how  it doesn't take an extensive knowledge  of the world of marvel to know that an  attitude like this is grossly  unbefitting of anyone calling themselves  captain america  even without seeing this exchange bucky  is well aware of this and when he  sam and zemo are on the plane leaving  majorpoor bucky tells sam he's going to  take steve's shield from walker once  their mission is over  the shield means too much to bucky to  see its importance and the legacy behind  it desecrated while it's in walker's  hands  bucky knows the world needs a new  captain america but not the one it has  right now  and he goes on to imply that he'd take  the title if need be  however sam now realizes he regrets  giving up the shield  and also wants to get it back to destroy  it neither of these two agree on what  should be done with a shield but they  both know it can't stay in walker's  hands  of course if you're looking to the comic  books for your answer you're out of luck  both the falcon and the winter soldier  have spent time using the name captain  america and carrying his signature  shield  bucky took the mantle first in 2008's  captain america vol  3 number 34 while sam started his stint  as captain america a few years later  in 2014's captain america volume 7  number 25.  at this point it's anybody's guess as to  which one of these two will wield the  shield by the series  end if either of them do so at all  having evaded the bounty on their heads  in madrapor sam bucky and zemo soon head  to latvia to learn more about carly's  connection to the late donya madani the  trio arrived there safely but bucky can  tell that something isn't quite right  he splits off from his allies and begins  retracing their steps  discovering tracking fobs that lead into  a nearby alley he reaches the end of the  fob's trail calling out for their owner  to reveal themselves in a magnificent  twist dura malaji member io emerges  explaining that she followed them to  latvia for zemo the connections between  zemo bucky and the entire nation of  wakanda date back to captain america  civil war  zemo was directly responsible for the  death of the wakandan king t'chaka  making him a target for the then prince  t'challa who sought revenge but zemo  pinned the bombing on bucky  leading him and the black panther to  clash thankfully by the end of the film  the plot came to light and t'challa  learned of zemo's treachery  the baron went to jail and bucky went to  live in wakanda to begin rehabilitating  himself after his time living as the  brainwashed winter soldier  it's hard to blame the wakandan people  for wanting zemo locked up once again  it'll be very intriguing to see how  wakanda and its people factor into the  next three episodes of the falcon and  the winter soldier now that they've made  their presence known  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite comic book heroes and  villains are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single  [Music]  one

